Description: GHSA-9qww-pwc4-77qq (CVE-2026-89160): pcre2_dfa_match() (\X, word boundaries, the rewind of a lookbehind) and the JIT \X read before the start of a UTF subject that was not checked there (it begins with continuation bytes, and a start offset is into it: a check of UTF covers only the part a match can reach); bounded by the checked part, as pcre2_match() is since 10.48. preg_* with /u, \X and an offset, with the JIT. Not fixed upstream (10.49 has the same code)
Origin: the patches of SUSE (Martin Schreiner, 10.09.2026, bsc#1277710, SLE 16 and Leap 16.0: pcre2-dfa-match-check-subject.patch and pcre2-jit-extuni-backchar-bound.patch), as they are on 10.49, the same as files/patch-GHSA-9qww-pwc4-77qq of devel/pcre2 of azsupport/ports; the paths those of ext/pcre/pcre2lib

